Phase 09 — Basic Spatial Translation Overlay

Objective

Display translated text directly on the Windows desktop near the source text.

Read First

Read:

* PROJECT_SPEC.md
* ARCHITECTURE.md
* PROJECT_STATE.md

Requirements

Create:

overlay/
├── overlay_window.py
└── overlay_renderer.py

Use PySide6.

The overlay should:

* be transparent
* have no unnecessary window chrome
* be visually readable
* not interfere with the underlying application
* support click-through behavior where practical
* support multiple translation regions

Initial Placement

For this milestone only:

source bbox
     ↓
translation
     ↓
place below source

Use a configurable gap.

Do not build sophisticated placement yet.

Example

Source:

今後のプロセス安全活動について

Overlay:

Future Process Safety Activities

The translation should appear spatially adjacent to the source.

Coordinate System

Clearly define:

* screen coordinates
* monitor coordinates
* overlay coordinates

Do not assume a single-monitor environment.

Tests

Test geometry conversion separately from actual GUI rendering.

Test:

* basic placement
* screen boundary clamping
* empty translation
* multiple regions

Completion

Run tests.

Perform a manual visual test if possible.

Update PROJECT_STATE.md.

Do not implement advanced placement.